html.append(f'<h2 id="executive">A. Executive summary</h2><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><b>{completed}</b>completed parameter-specific variants</div><div class="stat"><b>{len(count)}</b>analysis families</div><div class="stat"><b>1</b>proposed interaction analysis</div><div class="stat"><b>{len(figs)}</b>existing figure records</div></div>')
html.append('''<div class="callout"><b>The strongest recurring observation is a spatial difference under the site-weighted framework:</b> 328 has higher relative CLIP/SMI enrichment near the exonic side of splice landmarks. Common CPM and the tested pseudocount changes preserve its sign and location. <b>This is not universal robustness:</b> pooling reads before taking ratios reverses the mean direction, and peak selection/quantile normalization materially change effect magnitudes.</div>
<p>The full nonzero-peak analysis shows a small transcript-region effect, with more negative 324-minus-328 preference in 3′UTRs than introns. Quantile normalization preserves this direction and statistical detectability while reducing magnitude. Component diagnostics show contributions from both CLIP and SMI; background is not an inert denominator. The peak-proximity analysis does not support increased splice-boundary proximity among significantly enriched peaks.</p>
<p><b>Counting rule:</b> one row per saved combination of substantive selection, normalization, pseudocount, contrast, weighting or test framework. Plot formats, density versus ECDF, replicates, and landmark panels are not separate analyses. Round two contributes 30 peak configurations (10 selections × fixed P0.5 / fixed P0.1 / supported P0.5) and 30 metaprofile configurations (10 selections × raw depth / normalized depth / additive contrast). Fixed-nt and scaled-coordinate panels are grouped within each common round-two depth framework and explicitly described. Table-only sensitivities count as completed when numerical outputs exist. Two supported-only round-two rules remove no peaks and reproduce their full-universe counterparts; the registry flags these equivalent outputs. Thus the configuration count is not a count of independent results. Figures used solely as examples remain a grouped selected-display diagnostic.</p>''')
