html.append('''<h2 id="map">B. Analysis map and four questions</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>Q1 · Does CLIP-versus-SMI enrichment differ between constructs?</h3><p>Separate paired DESeq2 → descriptive effect comparison → strict / positive-selected peaks → all-nonzero continuous preference → quantile-normalized sensitivity → round-two peak configurations.</p><p>A direct count-model construct × assay interaction remains <b>PROPOSED / NOT YET RUN</b>.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Q2 · Where is the difference?</h3><p>Retained donor / acceptor / annotated-end windows → common-CPM site-weighted profiles → exon/intron side tests → coverage strata → expanded round-two windows and scaled intron/3′UTR coordinates.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Q3 · CLIP, SMI, or both?</h3><p>Common-CPM profiles → arithmetic CLIP and SMI coverage + exact mean-log component decomposition. Round-two additive differences are a separate quantity.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Q4 · How robust is it?</h3><p>Peak selection; full versus selected-library denominator; pseudocount; quantile normalization; equal-depth sampling; site versus pooled-read weighting; measurable-site masks; gene-stratified peak proximity.</p></div></div><p>Lineage arrows in the registry are methodological dependencies, not necessarily chronological order. Historical selections share the original CPM score calculation; their filtering lineage is shown separately from the later continuous-region analysis. <a href="analysis_relationships.tsv">Download exact parent/change/held-constant relationships</a>.</p>''')
